@startuml cls-configuration
title Class Diagram — Configuration

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle

class School <<external — academic>> {
}

class AcademicConfiguration {
  +configurationId: Int
  +schoolId: Int
  +configurationName: String
  +configurationValue: String
  +description: String
}

class SecurityConfiguration {
  +configurationId: Int
  +configurationName: String
  +configurationValue: String
  +description: String
}

AcademicConfiguration ..> School : school_id\n(cross-context, no FK)

note bottom of AcademicConfiguration
  Scoped per school (uq_academic_configuration
  on school_id + configuration_name), e.g.
  tardy_tolerance_minutes.
end note

note bottom of SecurityConfiguration
  Global (no school_id), uq on
  configuration_name, e.g. max_login_attempts,
  session_timeout_minutes,
  lockout_duration_minutes. Password policy
  lives in identity.password_policy, not here.
end note

note as N1
  BiometricUpdateCase is also physically hosted
  in this schema (transient hosting only, logical
  owner is Biometric — see cls-biometric.puml and
  AGENTS.md §4.6), so it is deliberately not drawn
  here. All classes above also carry the standard
  audit block (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at/
  created_by/updated_by/deleted_by/row_version) —
  omitted here for readability. See AGENTS.md
  §2.2 and 06-data/domains/08-configuration.md
  for the column-level ER view.
end note

@enduml
